# Every checkout gets the same bytes, on every platform.
#
# The Phase 0 contract in configs/phase0_gate.json pins SHA-256 hashes of files
# in this tree, and it hashes them as they sit on disk. Without this line,
# `core.autocrlf` decides those bytes and the contract stops meaning anything a
# second machine can check: the frozen map hash was recorded from a Windows
# checkout, so no clone on Linux could reproduce it, while a fresh clone on
# Windows could not reproduce the two blueprint hashes. Neither platform could
# verify the whole record. Frozen evidence has to mean the bytes in git, not
# one machine's rendering of them.
#
# It also keeps githooks/pre-commit runnable: a shell script checked out with
# CRLF fails with a bad-interpreter error on the `#!/bin/sh` line.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and said out loud rather than left to detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
